//! task: fix
//! ask: Keep a global counter and read it from a function.
//! expect: EXS-E0500
//! refs: §4.1 rule 7
//! explain: There is no module-level mutable state (§4.1 rule 7), so a `mutabilis` at module level is `EXS-E0500`. Module-level `firma` constants are legal; state that changes is a local, or a value passed in and returned.

mutabilis contor: u64 = 0;

publica functio f() -> u64 {
    redde contor;
}
//@ fixed
firma CONTOR: u64 = 0;

publica functio f() -> u64 {
    redde CONTOR;
}
